==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|conceptioun}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|conception}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|conceptio||a comprehending, a collection, composition, an expression, also a becoming pregnant}}, from {{m|la|concipere}}, past participle {{m|la|conceptus||conceive}}; see [[conceive]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/kənˈsɛpʃən/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-conception.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The act of [[conceive|conceiving]].
# The state of being conceived; the [[beginning]].
# The [[fertilization]] of an [[ovum]] by a [[sperm]] to form a [[zygote]].
# The start of [[pregnancy]].
# The formation of a [[conceptus]] or an [[implanted]] [[embryo]].
# The power or [[faculty]] of [[apprehend]]ing of forming an [[idea]] in the mind; the power of recalling a past sensation or perception; the ability to form [[mental]] [[abstraction]]s.
# An [[image]], idea, or [[notion]] formed in the mind; a [[concept]], [[plan]] or [[design]].

====Quotations====
* {{RQ:Authorized Version}}, Genesis 3:16
*: Unto the woman he said, I will greatly multiply thy sorrow and thy '''conception''' {{transterm|הרון|lang=he}}; in sorrow thou shalt bring forth children; and thy desire shall be to thy husband, and he shall rule over thee.

